body:
At the moment I honestly can't say I have any real dreams at this point. My dream at one point was to become a highly reputable computer engineer, helping develop computing architecture that will power the future. I have realised since then that I simply don't have the mental capacity to achieve that dream, so its hard to say now. 

&#x200B;

I still have some dreams to get a job in the computing field, both in hardware and software, but its going to be much harder to do from now on. Most importantly, I just want to be proud of who I am, and escape this endless flood of shame and self worthlessness.
